course: dictionary
lesson: 13781
title: Hard words with strong meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A long word can be easier to understand when you break it into parts. Intoxicate means to make someone drunk or affected by something. The ending -ation turns it into a noun that names a state. «The health lesson said alcohol and drugs can cause intoxication.» The words around it tell you the meaning: the state of not being able to think or move properly.
explain: Context clues can also tell you which meaning a word has. «The police said the driver was charged with driving under intoxication.» Driving is the clue here, and the law is involved, so this must mean being affected by alcohol or drugs. Always ask: what does this word need to mean in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «The crowd felt the intoxication of victory after the final goal.» Here there is no drink at all. The clues are victory and goal, so intoxication means a strong, dizzy feeling of joy. A good reader checks the whole sentence before choosing a meaning.
fact: Intoxication means being drunk, or affected by alcohol or drugs so that you cannot think or move properly.
fact: Intoxication can also mean being poisoned by a harmful substance.
fact: In a literary way, «intoxication» can mean a strong, dizzy feeling of joy, as if you were drunk with joy.
fact: «The intoxication of victory» means the wild, dizzy happiness of winning.
fact: Alcohol and drugs are dangerous for children, so never touch them, and tell an adult if you are worried.
exercise: «The health teacher explained that alcohol and drugs can cause intoxication.» What does intoxication mean here? | Feeling cold on a winter day | *Being affected by alcohol or drugs so that you cannot think or move properly | Being very kind to animals | Being very tired after a long walk
exercise: «The crowd felt the intoxication of victory after the final goal.» What kind of feeling is this? | *A strong, dizzy feeling of joy | A sleepy feeling after lunch | A cold, wet feeling | A feeling of being bored
exercise: «Driving under intoxication is against the law.» Why is this so dangerous? | Because the car is too small to steer | Because roads are always closed at night | *Because the driver cannot think or move properly | Because the sun is too bright to see
test:  What can intoxication mean, besides being drunk? | *Being poisoned by a harmful substance | Being very tall | Being very hungry | Being a fast runner
test:  Which sentence uses intoxication to mean a dizzy, happy feeling? | The nurse checked the boy for intoxication after the crash. | The bottle was labelled with a warning about intoxication. | The shop sells a drink that can cause intoxication. | *She felt the intoxication of winning the race, dizzy with joy.
exam: Mia says, «Intoxication means a sweet smell.» Is she right? | *No, it can mean being poisoned, or a dizzy feeling of joy, but not a smell | Yes, because it sounds sweet | Yes, it is a kind of perfume | No, it means being drunk, or affected by alcohol or drugs so you cannot think or move properly
